/* ================================
   Veloura Loader Screen
   path: src/assets/styles/04-components/veloura-loader.scss

   INTENTIONALLY EMPTY.

   The loading screen is styled by an inline <style> block inside
   src/views/layouts/master.twig, and that is on purpose: the loader has to be
   painted on the very first frame, before app.css has finished downloading.
   Styling it from this file would mean the loader flashes unstyled exactly
   when it is the only thing on screen.

   This file used to hold a full BEM stylesheet — .veloura-loader,
   .veloura-loader__bg and friends — but the markup uses .veloura-loader-bg,
   .veloura-loader-content and #veloura-loader-2026. Not one of those
   selectors matched anything, so all 150 lines were dead. The glass
   background was the visible cost: the only glass rule in the theme lived
   here, under a selector that never matched, so choosing "زجاجي" fell back to
   the flat colour painted by the inline block.

   The glass background now lives in master.twig with the other loader rules
   and reads the theme's shared glass tokens (--veloura-glass-surface,
   --veloura-glass-layer, --veloura-glass-filter), so it matches the rest of
   the store in both light and dark and needs no settings of its own.

   If loader styles are ever moved out of the template, they belong here —
